# KNOWN GAP (`todo/t1067`) — a closure that CAPTURES ANOTHER CLOSURE reads freed
# memory once the captured `Callable`'s scope ends. rc 0 with SILENTLY WRONG
# OUTPUT (a garbage integer); `AddressSanitizer: heap-use-after-free` in
# `__Closure_1__call` under `--sanitize`; `ggdef run` prints `41`.
#
# MECHANISM — THE CELL WITH NO SUBJECT. `c5` and the closure capturing it are
# both declared inside the loop body, so `c5`'s environment is freed at the end
# of each iteration while `outer` — assigned out of the loop — still holds a
# bitwise alias of it.
#
# Every other capture of a droppable value is closed by the ordinary
# consuming-position rule: clone if the source is live, move if it is dead.
# `Callable[T]` is the one type where NEITHER answer can be spelled. It is a
# ratified single-owner-by-design carve-out with no implicit-copy path in the
# lowering:
#
#   * an implicit CLONE breaches the carve-out;
#   * an implicit MOVE breaches it too, and silently consumes under D31
#     full-strict;
#   * a REJECTION has no fix-it the user can write — `(^c5)(int y): …` is a
#     parse error, `^(int y): …` is `E_ClosureKindMismatch`, and D7's
#     per-variable capture list (the construct that would let a user say
#     "capture `c5` by value") is UNIMPLEMENTED.
#
# ⇒ THE GATE IS D7, not the capture rule. Until a capture list exists there is
# nothing to widen the rule to. The consume-site validator carries a matching
# carve-out — `lacks_materialization_path` in `src/ir/validate.rs` — so this
# program still BUILDS rather than failing with a diagnostic no one can act on.
# That carve-out is why this file is a repro and not a red test.
#
# ⚠ THE INSTRUMENT IS C + ASan. The plain build is rc 0 and merely prints the
# wrong number.
#
# INTENDED (asserted by the `#[ignore]`d `known_gap_closure_capture_callable_block_scope_uaf`):
# prints `41`, rc 0, ASan-clean — the value `ggdef run` gives today.

void main():
    Callable[int()] outer = (): 0
    int n = 1
    while n > 0:
        int base = 41
        Callable[int()] c5 = (): base
        outer = (): c5()
        n = n - 1
    print(outer())
